<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Consolidation ability (decisions D195 and D205): what memory
  does while the cognition rests. The cognition
  (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx) invokes it as its child
  "consolidation" on entering rest, with the <param> memory (the address of
  the bot's memory; null: no memory), and leaving rest (any input) cancels it. It
  never identifies anyone (the conversation does, live, D194): it
  reinforces the people memory holds.

    consolidating { consolidating_from
      -> folding_pause -> folding_reading -> folding_from -> folding_writing
         -> folding_pause ...
      -> merging_pause -> merging_reading -> merging_from -> merging_refs
         -> merging_writing -> merging_pause ... }
      -> done (final) | failed (final)
    consolidating_from -no memory-> done

  Each step is one transaction of the bot's memory
  (abilities/memory/memory.scx, a request answered by its id, decision
  D265): a read, then a write guarded so that it
  commits only on the rows it read (a statement with an expected
  rowcount, which the sql and pgsql services check: a write whose guard
  does not hold fails and commits nothing). A step cancelled meanwhile
  (leaving rest cancels the invocation, and the service rolls the open
  transaction back) leaves nothing half-written, and the next rest begins
  again from what memory holds. Each step begins after a pause of
  step_pause_ms (consolidation.step.next): a memory step runs to its end
  within one call of the run, so the pause is where the run takes the
  input that arrived meanwhile, and input that leaves rest cancels the
  consolidation between two steps (it waits at most for the step in
  hand). A delay counts from the session time of the call that arms it,
  and a delayed send already due when a call's work ends fires in that
  call, so the pause must outlast a step (on a loaded machine too): 5 s
  by default, the bounds' consolidation_pause_ms overriding it.

  Folding (reinforcing identity): a person's representative voice
  (bot_person_centroid, kind voice: its compact text, its weight, the
  voices folded into it, and through_seq, the last of their
  bot_person_embedding rows folded in) takes in the voices heard for them
  since, at most fold_batch per step, oldest person first:
  <conversation:fold_voices> writes the unit vector of weight times the
  representative plus each voice's unit vector (a running mean of
  directions), and the write moves through_seq on, guarded by the
  through_seq it read. So identification (the conversation's identify)
  reads one compact row per person.

  Merging: two people whose representatives are at D90's threshold of each
  other (cosine 0.85 or more; <conversation:people_to_merge>, the most
  alike pair first) are one person: the newer is merged into the older
  (first heard first), in one transaction that writes the older's
  representative (both weighted by their weights; guarded by both
  representatives' weights and through_seq, and by neither having voices
  not yet folded) and re-points everything keyed on the newer person: their
  voices (bot_person_embedding), the short-term turns' speakers
  (bot_stm_turn speakers_json) and the short-term records (bot_stm_memory
  payload_json, source, target), every memory's content (cognitive
  episodes, relationship memories: bot_memory content) and subject_ref,
  and each relationship context reference that names them (bot_memory
  context_ref, recomputed by <conversation:merged_context_refs> to the
  bytes the conversation computes, at most merge_refs_limit), then deletes
  the newer person, guarded by no context reference naming them being left.
  A JSON text is re-pointed where it holds the person's ref as a whole
  string ("person-<n>" with its quotes); a ref inside another string (a
  session_ref's escaped context reference, which is provenance) is left
  as it was. A learned behavior's program is not rewritten: behaviors name
  events, not people. Merging ends when no two people are alike enough.

  Episodes: short-term turns are not turned into episodes here. Each turn's
  episode is already recorded by reflection (decision D97), and the
  short-term register (abilities/stm/stm.scx) sheds its turns by halves
  with no mechanism that makes episodes of them, so the seam is a step
  after merging (none yet).

  Bounds: steps (each write) at most max_steps per rest; each memory step
  within step_timeout_ms (consolidation.step.after). A memory failure, a
  timeout, an unmet guard or an error.* ends it in failed; the next rest
  begins again.

  Output (to the cognition, through done.invoke.consolidation):
  {folded, merged, steps, failed, reason}: the voices folded, the people
  merged, the writes made, and whether and why it failed (reason null when
  it did not, 'absent' when there is no memory). Logs: memory ('absent').

  Bindings: the conversation namespace package (the bot's memory, which
  the body invokes, binds the sql and pgsql service packages).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:conversation="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/conversation"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="consolidation" initial="consolidating">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The invoker's <param>: the address of the bot's memory (null: no memory). -->
    <data id="memory" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The id of each request this document last sent the memory, by
         the state that sent it (decision D265). -->
    <data id="memory_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The embeddings' kind consolidated (faces are D188's seam). -->
    <data id="kind" expr="'voice'"/>
    <!-- The voices one fold step reads (a voice's JSON text is about 5 KiB
         at 256 dimensions, under the sql service's 88 KiB result). -->
    <data id="fold_batch" expr="8"/>
    <!-- The relationship context references one merge re-points (the
         transaction's 64 statements less the merge's own). -->
    <data id="merge_refs_limit" expr="48"/>
    <!-- The writes one rest makes at most. -->
    <data id="max_steps" expr="256"/>
    <!-- The invoker's <param>: the bot's time bounds (its
         consolidation_pause_ms overrides step_pause_ms). -->
    <data id="bounds" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The pause before each step, where the run takes input: longer
         than a step takes, so that the run's call ends between two steps
         (a delayed send already due when a step ends fires in the same
         call, and input waits for the call to end). -->
    <data id="step_pause_ms" expr="5000"/>
    <!-- Each memory step's bound. -->
    <data id="step_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <!-- What was done. -->
    <data id="steps" expr="0"/>
    <data id="folded" expr="0"/>
    <data id="merged" expr="0"/>
    <data id="failure" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The step in hand: the rows read, the representative folded, the
         people to merge and their context references. -->
    <data id="rows" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="fold" expr="null"/>
    <data id="merge" expr="null"/>
    <data id="refs" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The statements (written for both engines). -->
    <data id="fold_select" expr="'SELECT c.person_id, c.centroid, c.weight, c.through_seq, e.seq, e.embedding FROM bot_person_centroid AS c JOIN bot_person_embedding AS e ON e.person_id = c.person_id AND e.kind = c.kind AND e.seq > c.through_seq WHERE c.kind = ?1 AND c.person_id = (SELECT d.person_id FROM bot_person_centroid AS d WHERE d.kind = ?1 AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bot_person_embedding AS f WHERE f.person_id = d.person_id AND f.kind = d.kind AND f.seq > d.through_seq) ORDER BY d.first_seq, d.person_id LIMIT 1) ORDER BY e.seq LIMIT ?2'"/>
    <data id="fold_update" expr="'UPDATE bot_person_centroid SET centroid = ?1, weight = ?2, through_seq = ?3, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE person_id = ?4 AND kind = ?5 AND through_seq = ?6'"/>
    <data id="people_select" expr="'SELECT person_id, centroid, weight, through_seq FROM bot_person_centroid WHERE kind = ?1 ORDER BY first_seq, person_id'"/>
    <data id="refs_select" expr="'SELECT DISTINCT context_ref FROM bot_memory WHERE context_ref LIKE ?1 ORDER BY context_ref LIMIT ?2'"/>
    <data id="merge_centroid" expr="'UPDATE bot_person_centroid SET centroid = ?1, weight = ?2, through_seq = ?3, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE person_id = ?4 AND kind = ?5 AND weight = ?6 AND through_seq = ?7 AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bot_person_centroid AS g WHERE g.person_id = ?8 AND g.kind = ?5 AND g.weight = ?9 AND g.through_seq = ?10) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bot_person_embedding AS e WHERE e.kind = ?5 AND ((e.person_id = ?4 AND e.seq > ?7) OR (e.person_id = ?8 AND e.seq > ?10)))'"/>
    <data id="merge_voices" expr="'UPDATE bot_person_embedding SET person_id = ?1 WHERE person_id = ?2'"/>
    <data id="merge_drop_centroids" expr="'DELETE FROM bot_person_centroid WHERE person_id = ?1'"/>
    <data id="merge_speakers" expr="'UPDATE bot_stm_turn SET speakers_json = REPLACE(speakers_json, ?1, ?2) WHERE speakers_json LIKE ?3'"/>
    <data id="merge_records" expr="'UPDATE bot_stm_memory SET payload_json = REPLACE(payload_json, ?1, ?2) WHERE payload_json LIKE ?3'"/>
    <data id="merge_record_sources" expr="'UPDATE bot_stm_memory SET source = ?1 WHERE source = ?2'"/>
    <data id="merge_record_targets" expr="'UPDATE bot_stm_memory SET target = ?1 WHERE target = ?2'"/>
    <data id="merge_contents" expr="'UPDATE bot_memory SET content = REPLACE(content, ?1, ?2) WHERE content LIKE ?3'"/>
    <data id="merge_subjects" expr="'UPDATE bot_memory SET subject_ref = ?1 WHERE subject_ref = ?2'"/>
    <data id="merge_context" expr="'UPDATE bot_memory SET context_ref = ?1 WHERE context_ref = ?2'"/>
    <data id="merge_person" expr="'DELETE FROM bot_person WHERE person_id = ?1 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bot_memory WHERE context_ref LIKE ?2)'"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="consolidation.js"/>

  <state id="consolidating" initial="consolidating_from">
    <!-- A memory step that fails, does not answer in time, or whose guard
         does not hold ends this rest's consolidation. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failed">
      <assign location="failure" expr="_event.data.message"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="consolidation.step.after" target="failed">
      <assign location="failure" expr="timeoutFailure()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="failed">
      <assign location="failure" expr="errorFailure(_event)"/>
    </transition>

    <state id="consolidating_from">
      <transition cond="isAbsent()" target="absent"/>
      <transition target="folding_pause"/>
    </state>

    <!-- Reinforce: the voices heard for one person since their
         representative was last folded. -->
    <state id="folding_pause">
      <onentry>
        <send id="fold-next" event="consolidation.step.next" delayexpr="pauseDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="fold-next"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="consolidation.step.next" target="folding_reading"/>
    </state>
    <state id="folding_reading">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="fold" expr="null"/>
        <send id="fold-read-after" event="consolidation.step.after" delayexpr="stepDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="fold-read-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.fold_read">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.fold_read"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="foldReadStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('fold_read')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="folding_from">
        <assign location="rows" expr="resultRows(_event, 0)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="folding_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoRows()" target="merging_pause"/>
      <transition cond="isBounded()" target="done"/>
      <transition target="folding_writing">
        <conversation:fold_voices location="fold" centroid="foldCentroid()" weight="foldWeight()" voices="foldVoices()"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="folding_writing">
      <onentry>
        <send id="fold-write-after" event="consolidation.step.after" delayexpr="stepDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="fold-write-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.fold_write">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.fold_write"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="foldWriteStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('fold_write')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="folding_pause">
        <assign location="folded" expr="foldedAfter()"/>
        <assign location="steps" expr="stepsAfter()"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- Merge: the two people most alike, the newer into the older. -->
    <state id="merging_pause">
      <onentry>
        <send id="merge-next" event="consolidation.step.next" delayexpr="pauseDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="merge-next"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="consolidation.step.next" target="merging_reading"/>
    </state>
    <state id="merging_reading">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="merge" expr="null"/>
        <send id="people-read-after" event="consolidation.step.after" delayexpr="stepDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="people-read-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.people_read">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.people_read"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="peopleReadStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('people_read')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="merging_from">
        <assign location="rows" expr="resultRows(_event, 0)"/>
        <conversation:people_to_merge location="merge" people="peopleRows()"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="merging_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoMerge()" target="done"/>
      <transition cond="isBounded()" target="done"/>
      <transition target="merging_refs"/>
    </state>
    <state id="merging_refs">
      <onentry>
        <send id="refs-read-after" event="consolidation.step.after" delayexpr="stepDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="refs-read-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.refs_read">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.refs_read"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="refsReadStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('refs_read')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="merging_writing">
        <conversation:merged_context_refs location="refs" refs="contextRefs(_event)" from="merge.from" into="merge.into"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="merging_writing">
      <onentry>
        <send id="merge-write-after" event="consolidation.step.after" delayexpr="stepDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="merge-write-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.merge_write">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.merge_write"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="mergeWriteStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('merge_write')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="merging_pause">
        <assign location="merged" expr="mergedAfter()"/>
        <assign location="steps" expr="stepsAfter()"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
  </state>

  <state id="absent">
    <onentry>
      <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition target="nothing"/>
  </state>

  <final id="done">
    <donedata>
      <param name="folded" expr="folded"/>
      <param name="merged" expr="merged"/>
      <param name="steps" expr="steps"/>
      <param name="failed" expr="false"/>
      <param name="reason" expr="null"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
  <final id="nothing">
    <donedata>
      <param name="folded" expr="0"/>
      <param name="merged" expr="0"/>
      <param name="steps" expr="0"/>
      <param name="failed" expr="false"/>
      <param name="reason" expr="'absent'"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
  <final id="failed">
    <donedata>
      <param name="folded" expr="folded"/>
      <param name="merged" expr="merged"/>
      <param name="steps" expr="steps"/>
      <param name="failed" expr="true"/>
      <param name="reason" expr="failure"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
